LeetCode 931


1. Problem Statement

You are given an n × n matrix.

You need to start from any cell in the first row and reach the last row.

From a cell (i, j), you can move to:

       ↙  ↓  ↘
      j-1 j j+1

So from the current cell, you can move:

directly down
down-left
down-right

You need to find the minimum possible sum of a falling path.

Example
[
 [2, 1, 3],
 [6, 5, 4],
 [7, 8, 9]
]

One minimum path is:

1 → 5 → 4

Sum:

1 + 5 + 4 = 10

Answer = 10.

2. 🧠 Intuition

Think about reaching a cell (i,j).

The previous cell can only be one of these three:

      ↙  ↓  ↘
   (i-1,j-1) (i-1,j) (i-1,j+1)
             ↓
           (i,j)

Therefore, to get the minimum path to (i,j), we choose the minimum path among those three previous cells.

So:

current minimum =
current value
+
minimum(
    upper-left,
    upper,
    upper-right
)

Main Logic :

matrix[i][0] += Math.min(
    matrix[i-1][0],
    matrix[i-1][1]
);

matrix[i][j] += Math.min(
    matrix[i-1][j-1],
    Math.min(matrix[i-1][j], matrix[i-1][j+1])
);

matrix[i][matrix.length-1] +=
    Math.min(
        matrix[i-1][matrix.length-1],
        matrix[i-1][matrix.length-2]
    );


Logic :

The problem is to find the minimum falling path sum from the first row to the last row. From each cell, I can move down, down-left, or down-right.

I use dynamic programming where matrix[i][j] represents the minimum path sum required to reach that cell from the first row. For each cell, I take its value and add the minimum of the three possible cells from the previous row. For the first and last columns, there are only two possible previous cells, so I handle those separately.

I update the input matrix itself instead of using a separate DP matrix, so I use O(1) extra space. Finally, I take the minimum value from the last row because the path can end at any column


Code :

class Solution {
    public int minFallingPathSum(int[][] matrix) {
        for(int i=1;i<matrix.length;i++){
            matrix[i][0]+=Math.min(matrix[i-1][0],matrix[i-1][1]);
            for(int j=1;j<matrix.length-1;j++){
                matrix[i][j]+=Math.min(matrix[i-1][j-1],Math.min(matrix[i-1][j],matrix[i-1][j+1]));
            }
            matrix[i][matrix.length-1]+=Math.min(matrix[i-1][matrix.length-1],matrix[i-1][matrix.length-2]);
        }
        int min=Integer.MAX_VALUE;
        for(int num:matrix[matrix.length-1]){
            min=Math.min(num,min);
        }
        return min;
    }
}
